    <KnowledgeArticle ElementID="HybridSolutionsCloud.HyperV.CsvAccessFailure.Alert.Rule" Visible="true"><MamlContent><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Summary</maml:title><maml:para>Failover Clustering event 5120 reports that I/O access to a Cluster Shared Volume is no longer available through the normal path.</maml:para></maml:section><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Operator response</maml:title><maml:para>Review the event text, CSV state and ownership, redirected I/O reason, storage paths, network paths, recent maintenance, and related storage latency. Restore supported paths before manually closing this event-based alert.</maml:para></maml:section></MamlContent></KnowledgeArticle>
    <KnowledgeArticle ElementID="HybridSolutionsCloud.HyperV.ClusterNodeRemoved.Alert.Rule" Visible="true"><MamlContent><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Summary</maml:title><maml:para>Failover Clustering event 1135 reports that a node was removed from active cluster membership.</maml:para></maml:section><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Operator response</maml:title><maml:para>Confirm whether the node was intentionally drained or maintained. Review cluster, network, heartbeat, quorum, and system events on all nodes. Confirm stable membership before manually closing this event-based alert.</maml:para></maml:section></MamlContent></KnowledgeArticle>
    <KnowledgeArticle ElementID="HybridSolutionsCloud.HyperV.CsvNoLongerAccessible.Alert.Rule" Visible="true"><MamlContent><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Summary</maml:title><maml:para>Failover Clustering event 5142 reports that a Cluster Shared Volume is no longer accessible from a cluster node.</maml:para></maml:section><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Operator response</maml:title><maml:para>Protect affected workloads, review the event text and CSV state from every node, validate storage and network paths, and correlate events 5120 and 1069. Confirm access is restored before manually closing this event-based alert.</maml:para></maml:section></MamlContent></KnowledgeArticle>
    <KnowledgeArticle ElementID="HybridSolutionsCloud.HyperV.ClusterRoleFailure.Alert.Rule" Visible="true"><MamlContent><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Summary</maml:title><maml:para>Failover Clustering event 1069 or 1205 reports a resource failure or a clustered role that could not be brought fully online.</maml:para></maml:section><maml:section xmlns:maml="http://schemas.microsoft.com/maml/2004/10"><maml:title>Operator response</maml:title><maml:para>Identify the failed resource and role, review dependency and resource-host events, check current ownership and failover policy, and correct the underlying resource condition before manually closing this event-based alert.</maml:para></maml:section></MamlContent></KnowledgeArticle>
  </KnowledgeArticles></LanguagePack></LanguagePacks>
